WEBVTT

00:03:28.204 --> 00:03:33.459
and become at risk
for the vortex of extinction

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:35.586
as their populations dwindle.

00:03:35.962 --> 00:03:40.383
Now, with genetic rescue,
we can reverse this extinction vortex

00:03:40.383 --> 00:03:43.010
by bringing a new genetic variation

00:03:43.052 --> 00:03:46.389
and increasing the long-term survival
of these populations.

00:03:46.722 --> 00:03:50.142
And that’s exactly what we did
with this Przewalski’s foal

00:03:50.142 --> 00:03:51.519
named Kurt.

00:03:51.519 --> 00:03:54.939
That's actually his surrogate
mother to the right.

00:03:54.981 --> 00:03:58.693
She's an American Quarter Horse,
a different species.

00:03:59.694 --> 00:04:03.406
But Kurt's genome is all wild horse.